  "final_text": "I fixed the bug and all 8 tests now pass.\n\nThe problem was in `minor_units()` in `invoicing/currency.py`. It lowercased the currency code before checking it against the list of currencies with no decimal places, but that list holds uppercase codes (`{\"JPY\", \"KRW\"}`). So JPY never matched and was treated as having 2 decimal places, which made yen totals print as `\u00a514,118.50` instead of `\u00a514,118`.\n\nI changed `currency.lower()` to `currency.upper()` so the check matches. No test files were changed."
